# What the image build may not see.
#
# The Dockerfile's COPY . . ships the whole context into a build layer, and
# BuildKit caches layers. Without this file .env and full database dumps were
# being copied into that cache on every build — and because each new dump
# changed the context, the layer never hit, so every `make up` rebuilt from
# scratch (review 16.09, Ops #6). The build needs go.mod, go.sum, cmd/ and
# internal/ (migrations are embedded from there); nothing below is read by it.
.env
.env.*
backups/
.git/
.github/
.cursor/
spike/
deploy/
docs/
*.md
*.excalidraw
Makefile
.golangci.yml
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.dockerignore
